{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22: Key reduction: d=sum(v)-vP, l_i=(v_i-d)+, h_i=min(v_i,d), y=p-l. F becomes 0<=y_i<=h_i, sum y=r=sum(h)-d. Nearest is projection of 0. For positive 3D caps, equality requires centroid coordinates equal; swap symmetry shows E[y_i]<E[y_j] iff h_i<h_j and h_i<r. Thus equality iff all h_i equal OR r<=min h_i. For strictly positive winner values this simplifies to vP<=min(v_i), or vP>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), or all winner values equal. Checking degeneracies next.' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22: Key reduction: d=sum(v)-vP, l_i=(v_i-d)+, h_i=min(v_i,d), y=p-l. F becomes 0<=y_i<=h_i, sum y=r=sum(h)-d. Nearest is projection of 0. For positive 3D caps, equality requires centroid coordinates equal; swap symmetry shows E[y_i]<E[y_j] iff h_i<h_j and h_i<r. Thus equality iff all h_i equal OR r<=min h_i. For strictly positive winner values this simplifies to vP<=min(v_i), or vP>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), or all winner values equal. Checking degeneracies next.' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The geometry gives a simple condition: with all three winner values positive, the points coincide exactly when the package value is at most the smallest winner value, at least the sum of the two largest, or all three winner values are equal. I’m checking boundary cases and a worked example before writing the proof."}}
