{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'tail -n 8 /work/board.md'","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22: Read problem; deriving an exact centroid/projection equality condition via capped simplex geometry. Will independently characterize all parameter regions and coordinate findings.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Key reduction: d=sum(v)-vP, l_i=(v_i-d)+, h_i=min(v_i,d), y=p-l. F becomes 0<=y_i<=h_i, sum y=r=sum(h)-d. Nearest is projection of 0. For positive 3D caps, equality requires centroid coordinates equal; swap symmetry shows E[y_i]<E[y_j] iff h_i<h_j and h_i<r. Thus equality iff all h_i equal OR r<=min h_i. For strictly positive winner values this simplifies to vP<=min(v_i), or vP>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), or all winner values equal. Checking degeneracies next.\n[argon] 2026-10-22: Read problem and sol's reduction. I am verifying the reduction y = p - p^VCG, checking the minimum-revenue face R = max(v_P, sum l_i), and checking all boundary/degenerate cases (e.g. R = sum l_i when v_P <= sum l_i, or v_i = 0, etc.) via Python and analytical proof.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Proposed final condition (nonnegative values): equality iff at least one winner value is zero, OR vP<=min(v_i), OR vP>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), OR vA=vB=vC. With all winners positive, centroid interior forces y coordinates equal; swap argument gives classification above. Opus/argon: please verify independently and flag concerns; I will draft shared answer.md with this theorem and example (vA,vB,vC;vP)=(1,2,3;2), centroid=(4/9,7/9,7/9), nearest=(2/3,2/3,2/3).\n[opus] 20:37 Working on it. Key reduction: R=v_P, F={sum p=v_P, VCG_i<=p_i<=v_i}; in x=p-VCG coords F = simplex{x>=0,sum=D} cut by caps x_i<=u_i=min(v_i,s), s=sum v - v_P. Claim: equal iff min(u_i,D) equal for all i (reflection argument). Verifying numerically, will draft answer.md.\n[opus] 20:38 Independently verified sol's condition by Monte Carlo (20k random instances, exact polygon centroid vs water-filling projection): matches except 2 near-boundary tolerance artifacts (deviation is O(eps^2)). Example (1,2,3;2) confirmed: gap 2/9 in coord A. My proof of strict ordering: swap map sigma_ij sends F∩{x_i>x_j} into F∩{x_i<x_j} when h_i<h_j; leftover {x_j>h_i} has positive area iff h_i<r. Agree sol drafts answer.md.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Drafted answer.md with full swap-integral proof, simplified exact condition, zero-value cases, and differing example. Please review shared file before final agreement. No need to duplicate drafting; independent verification most useful.\n[sol] 2026-10-22: Exact rational polygon-centroid vs capped-water-filling verification passed all 2,125 instances with winner values 1..5 and half-integer 0<vP<V. Draft theorem and differing example confirmed. Awaiting final review of answer.md; no outstanding mathematical concerns.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
